// Package refusal holds the pack gate's typed refusals: PlayRefusal for the
// play verb's retry (the api handler maps it to 400) and PolicyRefusal for
// the build executor (the enrich streams lane branches it before the failure
// ledger). One home for both is D1's one-vocabulary story made literal
// (playback-capability-gate): the gate's refusals share one token vocabulary
// — exactly the descriptor's state_reason tokens, minted by the single
// PackGate judge — so they share one shape vocabulary too, the same
// Reason-carrying error type at every seam the gate closes, instead of a
// per-package copy that could drift. (GATE-2 amendment, 2026-10-31: the
// types moved here from internal/api and internal/enrich so internal/api
// stays within its exported-symbol budget; names, shapes and semantics are
// unchanged.)
package refusal

// PlayRefusal is the typed refusal the Deps.Play closure returns when the
// pack gate refuses a retry (playback-capability-gate D4): the item's failed
// packaging run is not re-enqueued because the pack lane cannot serve its
// codecs. Reason is the gate token — exactly the descriptor's state_reason
// vocabulary (codec_not_opted_in | codec_unsupported) — and the api play
// handler maps the type to 400 with that token as the error code,
// retryable: false. It carries no token/credential material (INV4) — the
// refusal names a policy verdict, never an authorization fact.
type PlayRefusal struct {
	Reason string
}

// Error implements error; the message is the same honest sentence the 400
// body carries beside the code.
func (e PlayRefusal) Error() string { return "packaging refused: " + e.Reason }

// PolicyRefusal is the typed build-time refusal (playback-capability-gate
// D4): the PackItem seam returns it when the pack gate closes AFTER a job was
// already enqueued (the knob flipped between enqueue and build). It is a
// policy verdict, never a pack failure — the enrich streams lane persists the
// failed state with Reason (the gate's state_reason token) and writes NO
// pack_failed ledger row, so a knob setting never charges the flat 30-day
// cooldown and re-enabling the knob heals through the frontier with no
// manual step.
type PolicyRefusal struct {
	Reason string
}

// Error carries the reason verbatim — the descriptor's own state_reason
// token, so persisted documents and read-side refusals share one vocabulary.
func (e PolicyRefusal) Error() string { return "packaging refused by policy: " + e.Reason }
